{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013sdvWvLKq6EXDFWgSwbg1Y","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tApply response_language to all user-facing prose — narration between tool calls, status updates, progress notes, and findings included; preserve code, paths, and identifiers.\n2\t\n3\t<step name=\"verify_phase_goal_regeneration\">\n4\t**The one verification action for a phase (#5118, ADR-5057 Phase 4).** The verification owner\n5\troutes `stale` (and `missing`) to `execute-phase`; this file is what that route runs, and it is the\n6\tONLY place the verification sequence is written, whole and in this order: the `verify:post` hook\n7\tdispatch with the SECURITY threats-open gate (`verify_post_security_gate`), the code-review gate,\n8\tthe gap-closure parent-artifact close, the manifest-gated regression gate, the verifier dispatch,\n9\tthe covered-input fingerprint, and the owner's status read. Two workflows include it —\n10\t`execute-phase.md` step `verify_phase_goal` and `verify-work.md` step `complete_session` (a report\n11\trouted to `execute-phase`) — and both run every step below, in order, identically. There is no\n12\tper-caller branch; what stays in `execute-phase.md` is only its own bookkeeping (the wave summary\n13\ttable in `aggregate_results`, the roadmap/state writes after a `passed` verdict).\n14\t\n15\t**Inputs — one bundle for both callers.** The `gsd_run query init.execute-phase \"${PHASE_NUMBER}\"`\n16\tbundle (execute-phase loaded it in `initialize`; verify-work loads the same query before including\n17\tthis file). From it: `phase_dir` (`PHASE_DIR`), `phase_number` (`PHASE_NUMBER`),\n18\t`verifier_model`, `phase_req_ids`, `requirements_path`, `section_manifest`, `response_language`.\n19\tThe phase goal is the `**Goal**` of this phase in ROADMAP.md, loaded explicitly below as `PHASE_GOAL`\n20\t(`roadmap.get-phase --pick goal`, the query `verify-work/steps/mvp-uat-framing.md` uses) — the same\n21\tvalue for both callers, never left for the model to resolve. Resolve the rest the same way:\n22\t\n23\t```bash\n24\tIFS= read -rd '' GSD_ARGS <<'GSD_ARGS_END_1a3dd7e54833ff9a319819fc2c751606' || true\n25\t$ARGUMENTS\n26\tGSD_ARGS_END_1a3dd7e54833ff9a319819fc2c751606\n27\tGSD_ARGS=${GSD_ARGS%$'\\n'}\n28\t_GSD_SHIM_NAME=\"gsd-tools.cjs\"; _GSD_RUNTIME_ROOT=\"${RUNTIME_DIR:-$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel 2>/dev/null || pwd)}\"; GSD_TOOLS=\"${_GSD_RUNTIME_ROOT}/gsd-core/bin/${_GSD_SHIM_NAME}\"; _gsd_at() { for _p; do if [ -f \"$_p\" ]; then GSD_TOOLS=\"$_p\"; return 0; fi; done; return 1; }; _gsd_id_ok() { case \"$(\"$1\" runtime-identity --raw 2>/dev/null || true)\" in '{\"packageName\":\"@opengsd/gsd-core\"'*'}') return 0;; *) return 1;; esac; }; _gsd_homes() { set -- \"${CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR:-$HOME/.claude}\" \"${ANTIGRAVITY_CONFIG_DIR:-$HOME/.gemini/antigravity}\" \"$HOME/.gemini/antigravity-ide\" \"$HOME/.gemini/antigravity-cli\" \"${AUGMENT_CONFIG_DIR:-$HOME/.augment}\" \"${CLINE_CONFIG_DIR:-$HOME/.cline}\" \"${CODEBUDDY_CONFIG_DIR:-$HOME/.codebuddy}\" \"${CODEX_HOME:-$HOME/.codex}\" \"${COPILOT_CONFIG_DIR:-${COPILOT_HOME:-$HOME/.copilot}}\" \"${CURSOR_CONFIG_DIR:-$HOME/.cursor}\" \"${HERMES_HOME:-$HOME/.hermes}\" \"${KILO_CONFIG_DIR:-${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/kilo}\" \"${KIMI_CONFIG_DIR:-$HOME/.config/agents}\" \"$HOME/.agents\" \"${KIMI_CODE_HOME:-$HOME/.kimi-code}\" \"${OPENCODE_CONFIG_DIR:-${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/opencode}\" \"${PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR:-$HOME/.pi/agent}\" \"${QWEN_CONFIG_DIR:-$HOME/.qwen}\" \"${TRAE_CONFIG_DIR:-$HOME/.trae}\" \"${WINDSURF_CONFIG_DIR:-$HOME/.codeium/windsurf}\" \"${ZCODE_CONFIG_DIR:-$HOME/.zcode}\" \"${GROK_AGENTS_HOME:-$HOME/.agents}\"; for _h; do _gsd_at \"$_h/gsd-core/bin/${_GSD_SHIM_NAME}\" && return 0; done; return 1; }; if _gsd_at \"${_GSD_RUNTIME_ROOT}/gsd-core/bin/${_GSD_SHIM_NAME}\" \"${_GSD_RUNTIME_ROOT}/.claude/gsd-core/bin/${_GSD_SHIM_NAME}\" \"${_GSD_RUNTIME_ROOT}/.codex/gsd-core/bin/${_GSD_SHIM_NAME}\"; then gsd_run() { node \"$GSD_TOOLS\" \"$@\"; }; elif _gsd_homes; then gsd_run() { node \"$GSD_TOOLS\" \"$@\"; }; elif unset -f gsd_run; _G=\"$(command -v gsd_run)\"; [ -n \"$_G\" ] && _gsd_id_ok \"$_G\"; then GSD_TOOLS=\"$_G\"; gsd_run() { \"$GSD_TOOLS\" \"$@\"; }; else echo \"ERROR: gsd-tools.cjs not found at $GSD_TOOLS and no identity-proving gsd_run is on PATH. Run: npx -y @opengsd/gsd-core@latest --claude --local\" >&2; exit 1; fi; GSD_IDENTITY_STATUS=unverified; _gsd_id_ok gsd_run && GSD_IDENTITY_STATUS=ok; export GSD_IDENTITY_STATUS; [ \"$GSD_IDENTITY_STATUS\" = ok ] || echo \"WARNING: \\\"$GSD_TOOLS\\\" did not prove it is @opengsd/gsd-core - it is either a different package or an @opengsd/gsd-core older than the runtime-identity verb. See docs/how-to/diagnose-a-foreign-gsd-tools.md\" >&2; if [ -n \"${CLAUDE_ENV_FILE:-}\" ] && [ -n \"${GSD_TOOLS:-}\" ]; then printf \"export PATH='%s':\\\"\\$PATH\\\"\\n\" \"${GSD_TOOLS%/*}\" >> \"$CLAUDE_ENV_FILE\" 2>/dev/null || true; fi\n29\tTDD_MODE=${TDD_MODE:-$(gsd_run loop render-hooks execute:post --active-cap tdd)}\n30\t# #4772: this file is Read, not textually substituted - write the parent command's original argument string in place of $ARGUMENTS so --ws reaches the query.\n31\tGSD_WS=$(echo \" $GSD_ARGS\" | sed -nE 's/.* --ws +([A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*).*/--ws \\1/p' | head -n 1)\n32\tVERIFIER_SKILLS=$(gsd_run query agent-skills gsd-verifier ${GSD_WS:+--ws=${GSD_WS##* }})\n33\tCONTEXT_WINDOW=$(gsd_run query config-get context_window --raw 2>/dev/null || echo \"200000\")\n34\tPHASE_GOAL=$(gsd_run query roadmap.get-phase \"${PHASE_NUMBER}\" ${GSD_WS:+--ws} ${GSD_WS:+\"${GSD_WS##*[[:space:]]}\"} --pick goal)\n35\t```\n36\t</step>\n37\t\n38\t<step name=\"verify_post_security_gate\">\n39\t**`verify:post` hook dispatch and the SECURITY threats-open gate.** This runs BEFORE the verifier\n40\twrites (and fingerprints) the report, so the dispatch takes no `--after-fingerprint` — nothing is\n41\tfingerprinted yet, and gating on it here would be a no-op by construction (the allowlisted exception\n42\tin `scripts/lint-verify-lifecycle-writes.allowlist.json`).\n43\t\n44\t```bash\n45\tVERIFY_POST_HOOKS_JSON=$(gsd_run loop render-hooks verify:post --raw)\n46\tSECURITY_FILE=$(ls \"${PHASE_DIR}\"/*-SECURITY.md 2>/dev/null | head -1)\n47\t```\n48\t\n49\tDispatch every `kind == \"step\"` hook per @gsd-core/references/loop-hook-dispatch.md (skip when none). The secure-phase routing below applies when that specific hook is active.\n50\t\n51\tIf no active secure-phase step hook exists: skip.\n52\t\n53\tIf an active secure-phase step hook exists AND `SECURITY_FILE` is empty (no SECURITY.md yet):\n54\tInclude in the next-steps routing output:\n55\t```\n56\t⚠ Security enforcement enabled — run before advancing:\n57\t  /gsd-secure-phase {PHASE} ${GSD_WS}\n58\t```\n59\t\n60\tIf an active secure-phase step hook exists AND SECURITY.md exists: check frontmatter `threats_open`. If > 0:\n61\t```\n62\t⚠ Security gate: {threats_open} threats open\n63\t  /gsd-secure-phase {PHASE} — resolve before advancing\n64\t```\n65\t</step>\n66\t\n67\t<step name=\"code_review_gate\" required=\"true\">\n68\t**This step is REQUIRED to evaluate the capability hook.** When the code-review capability is active, auto-invoke code review on the phase's source changes. Advisory only — never blocks execution flow. Also dispatches advisory execute:post gate hooks (e.g. tdd.review-checkpoint).\n69\t\n70\t**Capability gate:**\n71\t```bash\n72\tEXECUTE_POST_HOOKS_JSON=${EXECUTE_POST_HOOKS_JSON:-$(gsd_run loop render-hooks execute:post --raw)}\n73\t```\n74\t\n75\tDispatch `kind == \"step\"` hooks per @gsd-core/references/loop-hook-dispatch.md. `ref.skill == \"code-review\"`:\n76\t\n77\tIf no active code-review step hook exists: display \"Code review skipped (code-review capability inactive)\" and proceed to gate dispatch.\n78\t\n79\t**Invoke review:**\n80\t```\n81\tSkill(skill=\"gsd-${ref.skill}\", args=\"${PHASE_NUMBER}\")\n82\t```\n83\t\n84\t**Report the