d Test Infrastructure table.\n71\tState B: Filesystem scan:\n72\t\n73\t```bash\n74\tfind . -name \"pytest.ini\" -o -name \"jest.config.*\" -o -name \"vitest.config.*\" -o -name \"pyproject.toml\" 2>/dev/null | head -10\n75\tfind . \\( -name \"*.test.*\" -o -name \"*.spec.*\" -o -name \"test_*\" \\) -not -path \"*/node_modules/*\" 2>/dev/null | head -40\n76\t```\n77\t\n78\t### 2d. Cross-Reference\n79\t\n80\tMatch each requirement to existing tests by filename, imports, test descriptions. Record: requirement → test_file → status.\n81\t\n82\t## 3. Gap Analysis\n83\t\n84\tClassify each requirement:\n85\t\n86\t| Status | Criteria |\n87\t|--------|----------|\n88\t| COVERED | Test exists, targets behavior, runs green |\n89\t| PARTIAL | Test exists, failing or incomplete |\n90\t| MISSING | No test found |\n91\t\n92\tBuild: `{ task_id, requirement, gap_type, suggested_test_path, suggested_command }`\n93\t\n94\tNo gaps → skip to Step 6, set `nyquist_compliant: true`.\n95\t\n96\t## 4. Present Gap Plan\n97\t\n98\t**Text mode (`workflow.text_mode: true` in config or `--text` flag):** Set `TEXT_MODE=true` if `--text` is present in `$ARGUMENTS` OR `text_mode` from init JSON is `true`. When TEXT_MODE is active, replace every `AskUserQuestion` call with a plain-text numbered list and ask the user to type their choice number. This is required for non-Claude runtimes (OpenAI Codex, Antigravity, etc.) where `AskUserQuestion` is not available.\n99\tCall AskUserQuestion with gap table and options:\n100\t1. \"Fix all gaps\" → Step 5\n101\t2. \"Skip — mark manual-only\" → add to Manual-Only, Step 6\n102\t3. \"Cancel\" → exit\n103\t\n104\t## 5. Spawn gsd-nyquist-auditor\n105\t\n106\tPrint: `◆ Spawning nyquist auditor... (runs in a subagent — no output until it returns, ~1–5 min; expected, not a freeze)`\n107\t\n108\t<!-- #2508 runtime-aware-dispatch -->\n109\t\n110\t> **Runtime-aware dispatch (#2508 Phase 4).** GSD workflows dispatch specialized subagents by role. Before dispatching on a built-in-only runtime (kimi-code — three built-ins only), resolve the role to a built-in via `gsd_run query resolve-dispatch-type --requested <role> --raw`. On named-dispatch runtimes (Claude/OpenCode/…) the role is returned unchanged; on kimi-code it maps to `coder`/`explore`/`plan` by role-suffix. The persona rides `${AGENT_SKILLS_<ROLE>}` (Phase 3) regardless. See @gsd-core/references/runtime-aware-dispatch.md.\n111\t\n112\t<!-- #2517 model-omit-on-inherit -->\n113\t\n114\t> **Model omission (#2517).** Omit the `model` parameter entirely when the value it would carry (`AUDITOR_MODEL`) is `\"inherit\"` or empty. An empty value 404s on runtimes without native tier aliases — the default on non-Claude runtimes. Omitting it inherits the orchestrator's model. See @gsd-core/references/model-profile-resolution.md.\n115\t\n116\t```\n117\tAgent(\n118\t  prompt=\"Read $HOME/.claude/agents/gsd-nyquist-auditor.md for instructions.\\n\\n\" +\n119\t    \"<required_reading>{PLAN, SUMMARY, impl files, VALIDATION.md}</required_reading>\" +\n120\t    \"<gaps>{gap list}</gaps>\" +\n121\t    \"<test_infrastructure>{framework, config, commands}</test_infrastructure>\" +\n122\t    \"<constraints>Never modify impl files. Max 3 debug iterations. Escalate impl bugs.</constraints>\" +\n123\t    \"${AGENT_SKILLS_AUDITOR}\",\n124\t  subagent_type=\"gsd-nyquist-auditor\",\n125\t  model=\"{AUDITOR_MODEL}\",\n126\t  description=\"Fill validation gaps for Phase {N}\"\n127\t)\n128\t```\n129\t\n130\t> **ORCHESTRATOR RULE — CODEX RUNTIME**: After calling Agent() above, stop working on this task immediately. Do not read more files, edit code, or run tests related to this task while the subagent is active. Wait for the subagent to return its result. This prevents duplicate work, conflicting edits, and wasted context. Only resume when the subagent result is available.\n131\t\n132\tHandle return:\n133\t- `## GAPS FILLED` → record tests + map updates, Step 6\n134\t- `## PARTIAL` → record resolved, move escalated to manual-only, Step 6\n135\t- `## ESCALATE` → move all to manual-only, Step 6\n136\t\n137\t## 6. Generate/Update VALIDATION.md\n138\t\n139\t**State B (create):**\n140\t1. Read template from `$HOME/.claude/gsd-core/templates/VALIDATION.md`\n141\t2. Fill: frontmatter (**set `status: validated`**), Test Infrastructure, Per-Task Map, Manual-Only, Sign-Off\n142\t3. Write to `${PHASE_DIR}/${PADDED_PHASE}-VALIDATION.md`\n143\t\n144\t**State A (update):**\n145\t1. Update Per-Task Map statuses, add escalated to Manual-Only, update frontmatter (**set `status: validated`**)\n146\t2. Append to the audit trail through the owning verb — it compares against the LAST `## Validation Audit` block and skips the write entirely when nothing material changed (#5105 R3; #4981: idempotence alone is insufficient for VALIDATION, whose content legitimately changes with the plan/SUMMARY set, so this call is made AFTER the Per-Task Map update above, not instead of it):\n147\t\n148\t```bash\n149\tgsd_run query verification.append-audit \"${PHASE_DIR}/${PADDED_PHASE}-VALIDATION.md\" \\\n150\t  --heading \"Validation Audit\" \\\n151\t  --rows \"{\\\"Gaps found\\\": {N}, \\\"Resolved\\\": {M}, \\\"Escalated\\\": {K}}\"\n152\t```\n153\t\n154\t## 7. Commit\n155\t\n156\t```bash\n157\tgit add {test_files}\n158\tgit commit -m \"test(phase-${PHASE}): add Nyquist validation tests\"\n159\t\n160\tgsd_run query commit \"docs(phase-${PHASE}): add/update validation strategy\" \\\n161\t  --files \"${PHASE_DIR}/${PADDED_PHASE}-VALIDATION.md\"\n162\t```\n163\t\n164\t## 8. Results + Routing\n165\t\n166\t**Compliant:**\n167\t```\n168\tGSD > PHASE {N} IS NYQUIST-COMPLIANT\n169\tAll requirements have automated verification.\n170\t▶ Next: /gsd-audit-milestone ${GSD_WS}\n171\t```\n172\t\n173\t**Partial:**\n174\t```\n175\tGSD > PHASE {N} VALIDATED (PARTIAL)\n176\t{M} automated, {K} manual-only.\n177\t▶ Retry: /gsd-validate-phase {N} ${GSD_WS}\n178\t```\n179\t\n180\tDisplay `/clear` reminder.\n181\t\n182\t</pro