{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0179WVVvSgKJfQLn5FYrMJjY","type":"tool_result","content":"737\t<step name=\"spawn_reviewer\">\n738\tCompute the review output path:\n739\t```bash\n740\tREVIEW_PATH=\"${PHASE_DIR}/${PADDED_PHASE}-REVIEW.md\"\n741\t```\n742\t\n743\t`DIFF_BASE` for agent context (in case the agent needs it) is already set by `compute_file_scope`\n744\tabove — reuse it verbatim rather than re-deriving it here. #3191/#3995/#3661: this MUST be the\n745\tSAME value the Tier-3 file-scope step and (#4209) the external reviewer-lane dispatch both use —\n746\tthe reviewer agent consumes `diff_base` exactly when `files:` is empty, i.e. the same fail-closed\n747\tscenario Tier 3 protects, so a second, divergent recomputation here would silently re-arm the\n748\tmis-scoping one tier down AND make the external lane review a different diff than the internal\n749\treviewer (a previously-latent bug #4209 made observable — see B3 in `.wolf/buglog.json`).\n750\t\n751\tBuild required_reading block for agent:\n752\t```bash\n753\tFILES_TO_READ=\"\"\n754\tfor file in \"${REVIEW_FILES[@]}\"; do\n755\t  FILES_TO_READ+=\"- ${file}\\n\"\n756\tdone\n757\t```\n758\t\n759\tBuild config block for agent:\n760\t```bash\n761\tCONFIG_FILES=\"\"\n762\tfor file in \"${REVIEW_FILES[@]}\"; do\n763\t  CONFIG_FILES+=\"  - ${file}\\n\"\n764\tdone\n765\t```\n766\t\n767\tBuild structural findings block for agent:\n768\t```bash\n769\tSTRUCTURAL_FINDINGS_BLOCK=\"\"\n770\tMAX_FINDINGS_SIZE=50000\n771\tif [ -n \"$FALLOW_JSON_PATH\" ] && [ -f \"$FALLOW_JSON_PATH\" ]; then\n772\t  # Normalize fallow's raw report into the compact {summary, findings[]} contract\n773\t  # the reviewer consumes (real fallow schema -> normalized findings).\n774\t  FALLOW_NORMALIZED_PATH=\"${PHASE_DIR}/FALLOW-normalized.json\"\n775\t  # gsd-resolve-lib begin fallow-runner.cjs (#5640): load helpers from the installed runtime, not the cwd\n776\t  _gsd_lib_probe=\"fallow-runner.cjs\"\n777\t  _gsd_rt=\"${RUNTIME_DIR:-$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel 2>/dev/null || pwd)}\"\n778\t  _gsd_gr=\"$(command -v gsd_run 2>/dev/null || true)\"\n779\t  case \"$_gsd_gr\" in /*) ;; *) _gsd_gr=\"\" ;; esac # a gsd_run shell function prints its bare name: not a path\n780\t  [ -n \"$_gsd_gr\" ] && _gsd_gr=\"$(dirname \"$(node -p \"require('fs').realpathSync(process.argv[1])\" \"$_gsd_gr\" 2>/dev/null || echo \"$_gsd_gr\")\")/lib\"\n781\t  GSD_LIB_DIR=\"\"\n782\t  _gsd_pick() { for _gsd_d; do if [ -n \"$_gsd_d\" ] && [ -f \"$_gsd_d/$_gsd_lib_probe\" ]; then GSD_LIB_DIR=\"$_gsd_d\"; return 0; fi; done; return 1; }\n783\t  _gsd_pick \"${GSD_TOOLS:+${GSD_TOOLS%/*}/lib}\" \"$_gsd_rt/gsd-core/bin/lib\" \"$_gsd_rt/.claude/gsd-core/bin/lib\" \"$_gsd_rt/.codex/gsd-core/bin/lib\" \"$_gsd_gr\" \"${CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR:-$HOME/.claude}/gsd-core/bin/lib\" \"${CODEX_HOME:-$HOME/.codex}/gsd-core/bin/lib\" || true\n784\t  if [ -z \"$GSD_LIB_DIR\" ]; then echo \"ERROR: fallow-runner.cjs not found in the GSD runtime (looked in ${_gsd_rt}/gsd-core/bin/lib (and its .claude and .codex forms), ${_gsd_gr:-next to gsd_run (not on PATH)}, ${CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR:-$HOME/.claude}/gsd-core/bin/lib, ${CODEX_HOME:-$HOME/.codex}/gsd-core/bin/lib); continuing without it.\" >&2; fi\n785\t  export GSD_LIB_DIR\n786\t  # gsd-resolve-lib end\n787\t  FALLOW_SRC=\"$FALLOW_JSON_PATH\" FALLOW_OUT=\"$FALLOW_NORMALIZED_PATH\" node -e \"\n788\t    const fs = require('fs');\n789\t    const { normalizeFallowReportFile } = require(require('path').join(process.env.GSD_LIB_DIR, 'fallow-runner.cjs'));\n790\t    const n = normalizeFallowReportFile(process.env.FALLOW_SRC);\n791\t    fs.writeFileSync(process.env.FALLOW_OUT, JSON.stringify(n, null, 2));\n792\t  \" 2>/dev/null && FALLOW_EMBED_PATH=\"$FALLOW_NORMALIZED_PATH\" || FALLOW_EMBED_PATH=\"$FALLOW_JSON_PATH\"\n793\t  FALLOW_JSON_SIZE=$(wc -c < \"$FALLOW_EMBED_PATH\" | tr -d '[:space:]')\n794\t  if [ \"$FALLOW_JSON_SIZE\" -le \"$MAX_FINDINGS_SIZE\" ]; then\n795\t    # Escape any literal closing tag before embedding; the closing tag literal is escaped to prevent prompt-structure breakage if a fallow finding's file path or message contains the sequence.\n796\t    SAFE_FALLOW_JSON=$(sed 's#</structural_findings>#<\\/structural_findings>#g' \"$FALLOW_EMBED_PATH\")\n797\t    STRUCTURAL_FINDINGS_BLOCK=$(printf '<structural_findings>\\n%s\\n</structural_findings>\\n' \"$SAFE_FALLOW_JSON\")\n798\t  else\n799\t    echo \"Warning: skipping structural findings embed (${FALLOW_JSON_SIZE} bytes > ${MAX_FINDINGS_SIZE} bytes). Re-run with narrower scope/profile if needed.\"\n800\t  fi\n801\tfi\n802\t```\n803\t\n804\tGather the capability review rules addressed to this reviewer (#4790): active `contribution` hooks with `into: code-reviewer`,\n805\tread from the loop point the review step is registered at (`workflow.code_review_point`, default `execute:post`). This is\n806\tadvisory by construction: any failure leaves the prompt without them and never blocks the review. The fragments are handed over once,\n807\tbelow, beside — never instead of — `${AGENT_SKILLS_REVIEWER}`:\n808\t```bash\n809\tREVIEWER_POINT=$(gsd_run query config-get workflow.code_review_point --raw 2>/dev/null) || REVIEWER_POINT=\"execute:post\"\n810\tcase \"$REVIEWER_POINT\" in execute:post|execute:wave:post) ;; *) REVIEWER_POINT=\"execute:post\" ;; esac\n811\tREVIEWER_HOOKS_JSON=$(gsd_run loop render-hooks \"${REVIEWER_POINT}\" --raw 2>/dev/null) || REVIEWER_HOOKS_JSON=\"\"\n812\tif [[ \"$REVIEWER_HOOKS_JSON\" == @file:* ]]; then REVIEWER_HOOKS_JSON=$(cat \"${REVIEWER_HOOKS_JSON#@file:}\" 2>/dev/null || true); fi\n813\t# A literal closing tag inside a fragment is escaped so third-party text cannot end the block early.\n814\tREVIEWER_CONTRIBUTIONS=$(printf '%s' \"$REVIEWER_HOOKS_JSON\" | node -e 'let s=\"\";process.stdin.on(\"data\",d=>s+=d).on(\"end\",()=>{try{const h=(JSON.parse(s).activeHooks||[]).filter(x=>x&&x.kind===\"contribution\"&&x.into===\"code-reviewer\"&&x.fragment&&