7\t\n848\tReview the listed source files at ${REVIEW_DEPTH} depth. Write findings to ${REVIEW_PATH}.\n849\tDo NOT commit the output — the orchestrator handles that.\n850\t${AGENT_SKILLS_REVIEWER}\n851\t\n852\t${REVIEWER_CONTRIBUTIONS}\")\n853\t```\n854\t\n855\t> **ORCHESTRATOR RULE — CODEX RUNTIME**: After calling Agent() above, stop working on this task immediately. Do not read more files, edit code, or run tests related to this task while the subagent is active. Wait for the subagent to return its result. This prevents duplicate work, conflicting edits, and wasted context. Only resume when the subagent result is available.\n856\t\n857\t**Agent failure handling:**\n858\t\n859\tIf the Agent() call fails (agent error, timeout, or exception):\n860\t```\n861\tError: Code review agent failed: ${error_message}\n862\t\n863\tNo REVIEW.md created. You can retry with /gsd-code-review ${PHASE_ARG} or check agent logs.\n864\t```\n865\t\n866\tDo NOT proceed to commit_review step. Do NOT create a partial or empty REVIEW.md. Exit workflow.\n867\t</step>\n868\t\n869\t<step name=\"commit_review\">\n870\tAfter agent completes successfully, verify REVIEW.md was created and has valid structure:\n871\t\n872\t```bash\n873\t# #4209 R5: remove the reviewer-lane run dir now that the agent has read every evidence path it\n874\t# cited (the agent ran to completion before this step, per `dispatch_reviewer_lanes` above) — a\n875\t# no-op when no reviewer lane was dispatched (LANE_RUN_DIR stays unset).\n876\tif [ -n \"${LANE_RUN_DIR:-}\" ]; then\n877\t  rm -rf \"$LANE_RUN_DIR\"\n878\tfi\n879\t\n880\tif [ -f \"${REVIEW_PATH}\" ]; then\n881\t  # Validate REVIEW.md has valid YAML frontmatter with status field\n882\t  HAS_STATUS=$(REVIEW_PATH=\"${REVIEW_PATH}\" node -e \"\n883\t    const fs = require('fs');\n884\t    const content = fs.readFileSync(process.env.REVIEW_PATH, 'utf-8');\n885\t    const match = content.replace(/\\r\\n/g, '\\n').match(/^---\\n([\\s\\S]*?)\\n---/);\n886\t    if (match && 