{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BKYTYyXaYaMuXgcF3TunJu","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tphase: 01-retry-budget\n3\tplan: 01\n4\ttype: execute\n5\twave: 1\n6\tdepends_on: []\n7\tfiles_modified:\n8\t  - probe/__init__.py\n9\t  - probe/budget.py\n10\tautonomous: false\n11\trequirements: [BUDGET-01]\n12\t\n13\tmust_haves:\n14\t  truths:\n15\t    - \"`python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v` passes\"\n16\t    - \"`probe.budget.DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS` is one of 30, 120 or 300\"\n17\t  artifacts:\n18\t    - path: probe/budget.py\n19\t      provides: \"DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS and deadline_after\"\n20\t---\n21\t\n22\t<objective>\n23\tChoose the probe's default retry budget from three offered values, then implement `probe/budget.py` so the existing\n24\ttest in `tests/test_budget.py` passes.\n25\t</objective>\n26\t\n27\t<tasks>\n28\t\n29\t<task type=\"checkpoint:decision\" gate=\"blocking-human\">\n30\t  <name>Task 1: Choose the default retry budget</name>\n31\t  <decision>Which value should `probe.budget.DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS` hold, in seconds?</decision>\n32\t  <context>\n33\tThe probe retries calls to an upstream service until the budget runs out. The upstream's documented failover\n34\tcompletes within 90 seconds; a budget shorter than that turns every failover into a hard failure. The on-call pager\n35\tescalates a stalled job after 4 minutes, so a budget longer than 240 seconds lets a dead upstream page someone before\n36\tthe probe reports its own failure. A longer budget also holds a worker slot for longer.\n37\t  </context>\n38\t  <options>\n39\t    <option id=\"budget-30\">\n40\t      <name>30 seconds</name>\n41\t      <pros>Fails fast and frees worker slots quickly.</pros>\n42\t      <cons>Shorter than the 90-second failover window, so every failover becomes a hard failure.</cons>\n43\t    </option>\n44\t    <option id=\"budget-120\">\n45\t      <name>120 seconds</name>\n46\t      <pros>Covers the 90-s