{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NeiEibmtc99E2hmyaDwVpp","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tphase: 01-retry-budget\n3\treviewed: 2026-11-02T00:00:00Z\n4\tdepth: standard\n5\tfiles_reviewed: 1\n6\tfiles_reviewed_list:\n7\t  - tests/test_budget.py\n8\tfindings:\n9\t  critical: 0\n10\t  warning: 2\n11\t  info: 2\n12\t  total: 4\n13\tstatus: issues_found\n14\t---\n15\t\n16\t# Phase 01: Code Review Report\n17\t\n18\t**Reviewed:** 2026-11-02\n19\t**Depth:** standard\n20\t**Files Reviewed:** 1\n21\t**Status:** issues_found\n22\t\n23\t## Summary\n24\t\n25\tReviewed `tests/test_budget.py` with `probe/budget.py` as context. Both tests pass (`Ran 2 tests ... OK`). I also ran mutations in a scratch copy under `$HOME/.cache` (since removed): budget set to 30, 300 and 150 each failed the first test. A literal `120` in `deadline_after` with the constant at 121 failed both tests. A literal `120` with the constant at 120 passed.\n26\t\n27\tWhat that establishes: the tests catch a wrong budget value and a wrong deadline formula. What it does not establish: that the budget value is correct (the 120 choice is unconfirmed by a human, per the disposition file), or any behavior of non-finite or non-float input.\n28\t\n29\tNo security issues or crashes. The defects are in the test design.\n30\t\n31\t## Warnings\n32\t\n33\t### WR-03: Budget test is self-contradictory and collapses to `== 120`\n34\t\n35\t**File:** `tests/test_budget.py:5,11-13`\n36\t**Issue:** `OFFERED_BUDGETS = (30, 120, 300)` is asserted as the acceptable set. The range assertions then require `90 < value < 240`, which excludes 30 and 300. The intersection of the two is `{120}`, so the test is equivalent to `assertEqual(..., 120)` spelled as three assertions. Verified by mutation: 30 fails on `30 not greater than 90`, 300 fails on `300 not less than 240`, and 150 fails on `not found in (30, 120, 300)`.\n37\t\n38\tThis conflicts with `01-REVIEW-DISPOSITION.md` (WR-01), which says an operator \"can override it by changing `probe/budget.py`\". Overriding to any other offered value (30 or 300) turns the suite red, so the override needs a test edit too. The test name says \"one of the offered values\" but it enforces one specific value.\n39\t\n40\t**Fix:** Decide what the test is meant to pin. Either pin the chosen value explicitly:\n41\t```python\n42\tCHOSEN_BUDGET_SECS = 120\n43\tself.assertEqual(DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS, CHOSEN_BUDGET_SECS)\n44\t```\n45\tor, if the contract is \"an offered value that satisfies the failover and pager constraints\", name the constraints and filter the offers by them:\n46\t```python\n47\tUPSTREAM_FAILOVER_SECS = 90\n48\tPAGER_ESCALATION_SECS = 240\n49\tself.assertIn(DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS, OFFERED_BUDGETS)\n50\tself.assertGreater(DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS, UPSTREAM_FAILOVER_SECS)\n51\tself.assertLess(DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS, PAGER_ESCALATION_SECS)\n52\t```\n53\tand drop or justify offered values the range can never accept.\n54\t\n55\t### WR-04: Deadline test restates the implementation and cannot tell the constant from a literal\n56\t\n57\t**File:** `tests/test_budget.py:16-18`\n58\t**Issue:** All three assertions compute the expected value as `start + DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS`, which is the implementation's own expression. The test shows `deadline_after` adds the constant. It does not show that it adds the constant rather than a hardcoded number: a literal `120` in `deadline_after` passes whenever the constant is also 120 (verified). The test also never checks an independent expected number, so its result depends on `DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS` being right, which is the other test's job. Three inputs (10.0, 0.0, -5.0) all exercise the same single code path.\n59\t\n60\t**Fix:** Patch the constant so the test is independent of its real value:\n61\t```python\n62\tfrom unittest import mock\n63\t\n64\twith mock.patch(\"probe.budget.DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS\", 7):\n65\t    self.assertEqual(deadline_after(10.0), 17.0)\n66\t```\n67\tThat fails if the function uses a literal or a stale copy of the budget.\n68\t\n69\t## Info\n70\t\n71\t### IN-03: Magic numbers 90 and 240 duplicate a comment in the source module\n72\t\n73\t**File:** `tests/test_budget.py:12-13`\n74\t**Issue:** The bounds come from the comment in `probe/budget.py:3-4` (90-second failover, 240-second pager escalation). The comment's figures cannot be checked from this repo (see disposition IN-01). The test copies them as bare literals, so the source and the test can drift without any link between them.\n75\t**Fix:** Name the constants as in WR-03, or export them from `probe/budget.py` and import them in the test.\n76\t\n77\t### IN-04: `assertIsInstance(..., int)` does not exclude `bool`, and no test covers input type or non-finite input\n78\t\n79\t**File:** `tests/test_budget.py:10,15-18`\n80\t**Issue:** `bool` is a subclass of `int`, so the isinstance check is weaker than it looks. Here the `assertIn` that follows makes it harmless, because `True` is not in the offered set. `deadline_after` is untested for `int` input (returns `int`, not `float`), `nan` and `inf`. The disposition file defers this because no caller exists yet. I agree it is latent, not a defect today.\n81\t**Fix:** Add edge-case tests when the first retry loop calls `deadline_after`. Until then, leave this as is.\n82\t\n83\t---\n84\t\n85\t_Reviewed: 2026-11-02_\n86\t_Reviewer: Claude (gsd-code-reviewer)_\n87\t_Depth: standard_\n88\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_017UaMjFgQwydoFHWyKdxihe","agent_id":"af4b934432737e3ed","session_id":"uuid-7","uuid":"uuid-690","timestamp":"2026-11-02T18:59:18.121Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NeiEibmtc99E2hmyaDwVpp","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"gsd-verifier","task_description":"Verify phase 01 goal achievement"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012WczsA6tv2JKgysNb3A895","type":"tool_result","content":"\"\"\"Default retry budget for the probe and the deadline it implies.\"\"\"\n\n# Covers the upstream's 90-second failover and reports before the pager\n# escalates a stalled job at 240 seconds.\nDEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS: int = 120\n\n\ndef deadline_after(start_secs: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Return the time at which a retry loop started at `start_secs` must stop.\"\"\"\n    return start_secs + DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS\n----\nimport unittest\n\nfrom probe.budget import DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS, deadline_after\n\nOFFERED_BUDGETS = (30, 120, 300)\n\n\nclass RetryBudgetTest(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_budget_is_one_of_the_offered_values(self) -> None:\n        self.assertIsInstance(DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS, int)\n        self.assertIn(DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS, OFFERED_BUDGETS)\n        self.assertGreater(DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS, 90)\n        self.assertLess(DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS, 240)\n\n    def test_deadline_adds_the_budget_to_the_start(self) -> None:\n        self.assertEqual(deadline_after(10.0), 10.0 + DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS)\n        self.assertEqual(deadline_after(0.0), DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS)\n        self.assertEqual(deadline_after(-5.0), -5.0 + DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    unittest.main()\n----\nbe16c47 test(01): sample deadline_after widely and pin the budget's range\n tests/test_budget.py | 4 ++++\n 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)\na3cd031 feat(01-01): add retry budget constant and deadline helper\n probe/__init__.py |  0\n probe/budget.py   | 10 ++++++++++\n 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+)\n5b9fb44 chore: scaffold devflow live-run payload\n tests/test_budget.py | 18 ++++++++++++++++++\n 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)\n---\nbe16c47 DevFlow Probe Mon Nov 2 13:52:39 2026 -0500 test(01): sample deadline_after widely and pin the budget's range\n\n\n tests/test_budget.py | 4 ++++\n 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)\ncommit be16c47f85247f931ac6b6fe8a0a563b46332017\nAuthor: DevFlow Probe <devflow-probe@localhost>\nDate:   Mon Nov 2 13:52:39 2026 -0500\n\n    test(01): sample deadline_after widely and pin the budget's range\n\ndiff --git a/tests/test_budget.py b/tests/test_budget.py\nindex 5192c78..2d40fb8 100644\n--- a/tests/test_budget.py\n+++ b/tests/test_budget.py\n@@ -9,9 +9,13 @@ class RetryBudgetTest(unittest.TestCase):\n     def test_budget_is_one_of_the_offered_values(self) -> None:\n         self.assertIsInstance(DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS, int)\n         self.assertIn(DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS, OFFERED_BUDGETS)\n+        self.assertGreater(DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS, 90)\n+        self.assertLess(DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS, 240)\n \n     def test_deadline_adds_the_budget_to_the_start(self) -> None:\n         self.assertEqual(deadline_after(10.0), 10.0 + DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS)\n+        self.assertEqual(deadline_after(0.0), DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS)\n+        self.assertEqual(deadline_after(-5.0), -5.0 + DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS)\n \n \n if __name__ == \"__main__\":","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_017UaMjFgQwydoFHWyKdxihe","agent_id":"af4b934432737e3ed","session_id":"uuid-7","uuid":"uuid-691","timestamp":"2026-11-02T18:59:20.567Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012WczsA6tv2JKgysNb3A895","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"gsd-verifier","task_description":"Verify phase 01 goal achievement"}
